# Backend and SQL location

The backend is the **sibling** folder `../New_Joscity` (under `Downloads/apps`), **not** `JosCity-App/New_Joscity`.

The live **web frontend** served at localhost:5173 is the sibling folder `../JOSCITY`, **not** `JosCity-App/JOSCITY`.

Correct backend: `C:\Users\HP OMEN\Downloads\apps\New_Joscity`
Correct web UI: `C:\Users\HP OMEN\Downloads\apps\JOSCITY`
Wrong: `C:\Users\HP OMEN\Downloads\apps\JosCity-App\New_Joscity` or `JosCity-App\JOSCITY` for the running Vite app.

Correct: `C:\Users\HP OMEN\Downloads\apps\New_Joscity`
Wrong: `C:\Users\HP OMEN\Downloads\apps\JosCity-App\New_Joscity`

Never put API handlers, routes, or SQL in `JosCity-App/New_Joscity`, `mobile`, or `JOSCITY`.

## Backend

- Add or update controllers, routes, services, and middleware only under `../New_Joscity/`
- Wire new endpoints in `../New_Joscity/server.js` and `../New_Joscity/routes/`
- If a mobile or web feature needs an API, implement it in `../New_Joscity` first, then call it from the client

## PostgreSQL

- Add numbered files under `../New_Joscity/migrations/`
- Keep changes additive and idempotent (`IF NOT EXISTS`, `ON CONFLICT`)
- Run migrations from that folder: `cd ../New_Joscity` then `npm run migrate -- migrations/<file>.sql`

```text
../New_Joscity/
  controller/
  routes/
  services/
  migrations/027_feature_name.sql
```
